WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.395
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:07.665 --> 00:09.025
SAY NO TO PIRACY, SUPPORT ORIGINALS

3
01:43.185 --> 01:44.305
‎-Good morning. ‎-Good morning.

4
01:44.385 --> 01:45.665
‎-Good morning. ‎-Good morning.

5
01:45.745 --> 01:47.585
‎-Okay. ‎-Good.

6
01:49.265 --> 01:50.265
Morning.

7
01:50.785 --> 01:51.745
You keep pushing this hard.

8
01:51.825 --> 01:52.985
Not afraid of a heart attack?

9
01:54.385 --> 01:55.465
Right back at you.

10
01:55.545 --> 01:58.265
Weren't you sending files in the group chat until 2 a.m.?

11
01:58.345 --> 01:59.265
Coffee?

12
01:59.785 --> 02:00.625
Sure.

13
02:02.625 --> 02:03.825
I can't compete with you.

14
02:03.905 --> 02:06.865
You're the only newbie who's landed a project on your own.

15
02:06.945 --> 02:10.024
It's just project initiation follow-up,

16
02:10.545 --> 02:12.545
writing technical specs and proposals.

17
02:12.625 --> 02:15.105
Once the contract is signed, a project manager will take over.

18
02:15.185 --> 02:17.225
We grunts just get to do the scut work.

19
02:18.585 --> 02:19.745
What else?

20
02:19.825 --> 02:21.185
You want to take over the whole project?

21
02:24.785 --> 02:27.145
I just got the Bolo Culture project.

22
02:27.225 --> 02:29.105
Quit being snarky first thing in the morning.

23
02:29.185 --> 02:31.025
Aren't you aiming to be a partner?

24
02:31.105 --> 02:32.265
Why take an interest in my small-scale project?

25
02:33.385 --> 02:34.705
I'm heading down.

26
02:34.785 --> 02:36.265
Of course I don't care.

27
02:37.465 --> 02:38.865
But don't act weak.

28
02:38.945 --> 02:40.425
Doesn't fit your image.

29
02:41.025 --> 02:44.025
Bring out that killer instinct you used to poach Lin Long's project.

30
02:44.945 --> 02:45.945
I like it.

31
02:51.105 --> 02:52.145
You two…?

32
02:54.065 --> 02:55.065
Go on.

33
02:56.305 --> 02:58.145
I'm grabbing breakfast downstairs. Need anything?

34
02:59.145 --> 03:01.265
-She likes the chicken breast panini. -Got it.

35
03:02.025 --> 03:02.865
Thanks.

36
03:04.425 --> 03:07.665
What do you get out of spilling my private business?

37
03:09.025 --> 03:10.985
At least it makes people think we're friends.

38
03:11.065 --> 03:13.385
Keeps the Deng Anran types off my back.

39
03:13.465 --> 03:14.945
Work itself is exhausting enough.

40
03:15.025 --> 03:18.225
I don't have the energy for office drama dumber

41
03:18.305 --> 03:19.385
than a soap opera.

42
03:19.985 --> 03:20.905
Smart.

43
03:22.385 --> 03:23.625
But let's get one thing straight.

44
03:24.305 --> 03:25.945
I'm keeping you as my right hand,

45
03:26.545 --> 03:27.785
not my friend.

46
03:29.145 --> 03:31.985
Okay by me. Right hand means trust.

47
03:43.345 --> 03:45.225
Actually, I've always wondered.

48
03:45.745 --> 03:48.785
We only met when we joined the company, so why have you always been

49
03:49.385 --> 03:50.665
so nice to me?

50
03:50.745 --> 03:51.985
Because I like you.

51
03:55.345 --> 03:56.545
You really don't remember?

52
03:58.345 --> 03:59.185
Remember what?

53
04:05.625 --> 04:08.385
Back in the day, by Daming Lake,

54
04:09.145 --> 04:10.425
you were Xia Yuhe.

55
04:11.945 --> 04:13.985
Oh my God. You actually tell jokes.

56
04:21.905 --> 04:22.865
Are you okay?

57
04:31.785 --> 04:32.705
Hello?

58
04:32.785 --> 04:34.025
Did you zone out?

59
04:37.185 --> 04:38.025
No.

60
04:38.545 --> 04:40.665
I was just thinking

61
04:41.385 --> 04:43.345
about how many newbies

62
04:43.425 --> 04:45.145
will actually show up for the weekend outdoor challenge.

63
04:46.105 --> 04:47.225
How many?

64
04:47.945 --> 04:49.425
All that overtime fried your brain?

65
04:49.505 --> 04:52.185
Didn't you see both newbie teams are gone?

66
04:54.545 --> 04:56.625
The three-month mark is the first hurdle.

67
05:02.465 --> 05:03.305
New colleagues,

68
05:03.385 --> 05:05.945
the rules for this new hire challenge are straightforward.

69
05:06.025 --> 05:08.585
Use your strategy and your courage.

70
05:08.665 --> 05:11.265
First team to reach the finish line wins.

71
05:11.345 --> 05:14.025
The winning team

72
05:14.105 --> 05:18.665
gets a two-week training at the North America HQ at year-end.

73
05:19.265 --> 05:20.545
Great!

74
05:20.625 --> 05:22.185
You each have a hand-drawn map.

75
05:22.265 --> 05:23.505
Mountain route, water route, and forest route.

76
05:23.585 --> 05:25.145
Each team can choose their own path.

77
05:25.225 --> 05:27.305
The goal is to reach the destination fast and efficiently.

78
05:27.385 --> 05:30.265
Each team has a professional outdoor guide for safety.

79
05:30.345 --> 05:32.585
Lu Le and I will supervise to ensure fairness.

80
05:32.665 --> 05:34.145
Other than that, you're on your own.

81
05:34.225 --> 05:35.865
-Move! -Good luck.

82
05:35.945 --> 05:36.865
-Go! -Go!

83
05:36.945 --> 05:37.945
MAXMISE CONSULTING STORM CHALLENGE CAMP

84
05:42.905 --> 05:43.825
Want to race?

85
05:44.345 --> 05:46.305
If you lose, we switch places.

86
05:46.385 --> 05:48.705
I'll be the partner, and you're the right hand.

87
05:49.585 --> 05:52.825
You know, your name is pretty good.

88
05:52.905 --> 05:54.065
"Chi" means being late. Great omen!

89
05:55.345 --> 05:56.665
See you at the finish line.

90
05:56.745 --> 05:58.185
-Off we go! -Let's go.

91
06:00.505 --> 06:01.785
Sorry.

92
06:02.785 --> 06:03.625
Tianna!

93
06:03.705 --> 06:04.585
Hurry!

94
06:20.065 --> 06:21.025
Thanks.

95
06:21.105 --> 06:22.705
This trekking pole is non-slip. Take it.

96
06:23.545 --> 06:25.465
I'm fine. I just didn't see the path clearly.

97
06:25.545 --> 06:26.385
Aren't you trying to win?

98
06:26.465 --> 06:28.305
If you slip and get hurt, you can't win.

99
06:28.385 --> 06:30.425
I'm not on the team. I don't have to walk.

100
06:32.585 --> 06:33.745
Okay.

101
06:33.825 --> 06:34.945
I'll return it in a bit.

102
06:35.025 --> 06:36.825
No need to be so formal with me.

103
06:49.585 --> 06:51.225
You're not going to hold the whole team back, are you?

104
07:03.265 --> 07:04.185
No need.

105
07:06.025 --> 07:07.985
I know first aid. I'll do it myself.

106
07:12.865 --> 07:13.705
Come on.

107
07:14.705 --> 07:16.585
You know first aid for helping others.

108
07:17.185 --> 07:19.265
Not so easy when it's yourself, is it?

109
07:20.425 --> 07:21.265
Here.

110
07:26.465 --> 07:29.505
Seriously, why are you so guarded?

111
07:31.225 --> 07:33.585
You really think everyone is after your dad's money?

112
07:36.025 --> 07:37.305
Red team!

113
07:37.385 --> 07:38.225
-Coming. -Coming.

114
07:38.305 --> 07:39.545
Let's talk it over.

115
07:39.625 --> 07:40.465
I just checked the map.

116
07:40.545 --> 07:42.385
Why don't we take the mountain route?

117
07:42.465 --> 07:43.465
The water route is shorter,

118
07:43.545 --> 07:45.425
but the current's too strong. It's kind of dangerous.

119
07:45.505 --> 07:48.785
There's a bridge up ahead that leads to the mountain path.

120
07:48.865 --> 07:50.265
It adds about three kilometers.

121
07:50.345 --> 07:51.585
But I think we might actually be faster that way.

122
07:51.665 --> 07:53.025
What do you all think?

123
07:53.105 --> 07:54.225
-Sure. It's fine with me. -Sounds good.

124
07:58.505 --> 08:01.825
The red team excels at analyzing materials and has strong command over projects.

125
08:01.905 --> 08:03.305
I took a look.

126
08:03.385 --> 08:06.065
Everyone on the team has to reach the finish line together to win,

127
08:06.145 --> 08:08.105
but my foot's injured. I can't go far.

128
08:08.185 --> 08:10.625
The water route is tough, but it's the shortest.

129
08:10.705 --> 08:11.705
Everyone, get your ropes out.

130
08:11.785 --> 08:12.825
-Okay. -Okay.

131
08:12.905 --> 08:15.065
The blue team has strong leadership

132
08:15.585 --> 08:17.185
and is good at handling pressure and working together.

133
08:17.265 --> 08:20.305
The yellow team has great team spirit.

134
08:20.385 --> 08:22.865
I've posted everyone's scores in the group chat.

135
08:22.945 --> 08:23.785
Check them out.

136
08:24.665 --> 08:26.425
The blue team's taking the shortcut across the stream.

137
08:26.505 --> 08:27.865
Tell them to stay safe.

138
08:27.945 --> 08:31.145
Don't worry. The guide said Bu Tianna looks professionally trained.

139
08:31.225 --> 08:32.185
It should be fine.

140
08:32.784 --> 08:34.904
They've all secured their safety ropes, bu Tianna's bringing up the rear.

141
08:34.985 --> 08:37.105
Most of the team has already crossed safely.

142
09:23.065 --> 09:25.025
-Keep going! -Go!

143
09:25.105 --> 09:27.185
-You got this! -Here, drink some water.

144
09:27.265 --> 09:28.505
Almost there! Come on!

145
09:28.585 --> 09:30.545
-Nice work. -Keep going!

146
09:30.625 --> 09:31.625
-Almost there! -Where are they?

147
09:31.705 --> 09:32.585
-Zhao Heng. Tianna. -Keep going!

148
09:32.665 --> 09:34.025
-Come on! -Come on!

149
09:34.105 --> 09:37.025
-Keep going! -Almost there!

150
09:37.745 --> 09:39.065
Su Su, come on!

151
09:39.145 --> 09:40.585
-Su Su, go! -Go!

152
09:40.665 --> 09:43.145
-Su Su, come on! -Su Su, come on!

153
09:43.225 --> 09:44.425
-Go for it! -Go for it!

154
09:44.505 --> 09:45.625
Zhao Heng, Tianna, come on!

155
09:45.705 --> 09:46.545
Su Su!

156
09:46.625 --> 09:48.705
‎-Come on! ‎-Go!

157
09:48.785 --> 09:50.745
‎-Come on! ‎-Go!

158
09:50.825 --> 09:52.905
Su Su, come on! Su Su, you've got this!

159
09:52.985 --> 09:53.865
-Go! -Go!

160
09:55.065 --> 09:58.065
‎You got this!

161
09:59.785 --> 10:00.785
Come on.

162
10:01.425 --> 10:02.265
Get on my back. Hop on.

163
10:02.345 --> 10:04.785
This isn't for you. It's for the whole team.

164
10:05.385 --> 10:06.425
Come on!

165
10:10.025 --> 10:11.065
Go!

166
10:11.585 --> 10:12.985
-Let's go! -Let's go!

167
10:13.065 --> 10:15.185
-Su Su, come on! -Su Su, come on!

168
10:15.265 --> 10:16.425
-You got this! -You got this!

169
10:20.745 --> 10:21.865
Almost there!

170
10:21.945 --> 10:23.465
-Go, go! -Go, go!

171
10:23.545 --> 10:25.385
-Go for it! -Go for it!

172
10:26.185 --> 10:27.985
MAXMISE CONSULTING STORM CHALLENGE CAMP FINISH LINE

173
10:31.865 --> 10:33.025
Nice.

174
10:33.625 --> 10:35.225
Are you okay? You did great.

175
10:35.825 --> 10:36.865
Well done.

176
10:38.865 --> 10:40.785
Congratulations to our champions, blue team!

177
10:47.825 --> 10:50.025
This event is officially a success.

178
10:50.105 --> 10:51.905
Thanks to everyone for giving it your all!

179
11:01.785 --> 11:02.625
Did you make this?

180
11:03.425 --> 11:06.225
This looks like a commercial. Nice work.

181
11:06.305 --> 11:08.065
It's not that I did anything amazing.

182
11:08.145 --> 11:10.105
It's just that everyone's emotions were so real.

183
11:10.705 --> 11:14.185
They call it building team spirit,

184
11:14.265 --> 11:16.065
trust, and courage.

185
11:16.145 --> 11:16.985
But really,

186
11:17.065 --> 11:19.665
they just want us to get high on that sense of satisfaction

187
11:19.745 --> 11:21.105
from overcoming challenges.

188
11:21.185 --> 11:23.025
And you know what? We totally fall for it.

189
11:53.905 --> 11:54.745
Hey,

190
11:55.585 --> 11:57.025
I took some photos of you back there.

191
11:57.105 --> 11:58.505
Let me add you on WeChat and send them over.

192
12:03.625 --> 12:04.545
ZHAO HENG, ADD TO CONTACTS

193
12:12.385 --> 12:13.065
ADD IMAGE TO REMARK

194
12:26.425 --> 12:27.265
Nice shots.

195
12:28.065 --> 12:29.465
Free for lunch? My treat.

196
12:39.625 --> 12:40.825
So good!

197
12:42.505 --> 12:44.065
Fancy restaurants really are different.

198
12:44.145 --> 12:45.705
Great atmosphere. Great food.

199
12:46.505 --> 12:47.945
How did you know I love lamb chops?

200
12:48.625 --> 12:50.025
It's perfect for me!

201
12:50.785 --> 12:53.305
When I was a kid, I herded sheep on those Northwestern hillsides.

202
12:53.385 --> 12:55.025
Blue skies. Green grass.

203
12:55.105 --> 12:56.545
Very pastoral.

204
12:57.065 --> 12:59.865
But even the best view can't fill your stomach.

205
12:59.945 --> 13:02.905
Back then, my family didn't have much.

206
13:02.985 --> 13:04.465
All I had for lunch every day was a dry mantou.

207
13:04.545 --> 13:05.665
No way that was enough.

208
13:05.745 --> 13:10.105
So from then on, I'd stare at those little bleating sheep

209
13:10.625 --> 13:13.905
and swear that once I got to college, I'd eat all the lamb I wanted.

210
13:14.865 --> 13:16.265
Well? Pretty good story?

211
13:17.985 --> 13:18.945
Pretty good.

212
13:19.025 --> 13:21.385
But the better part is still coming.

213
13:21.465 --> 13:22.825
Let me borrow your phone.

214
13:22.905 --> 13:23.745
Unlock it.

215
13:35.625 --> 13:36.305
‎CHOOSE PICTURES

216
13:37.665 --> 13:38.825
DELETED

217
13:40.785 --> 13:43.025
Last time I borrowed your ice pack and bandages

218
13:43.105 --> 13:44.745
and you carried me.

219
13:44.825 --> 13:47.105
So today I bought you lunch and kept you company.

220
13:47.185 --> 13:49.345
Materially and emotionally, we're even.

221
13:49.425 --> 13:51.985
And I already deleted those photos of me on your phone.

222
13:52.065 --> 13:53.065
Stop sneaking photos of me from now on.

223
13:53.145 --> 13:54.585
If you do it again,

224
13:54.665 --> 13:56.745
I'll report you to the company for harassment.

225
13:56.825 --> 13:57.705
Bye.

226
13:58.305 --> 14:00.385
I've sent you the 3,000 for the lunch bill.

227
14:00.465 --> 14:02.545
Wait, I wasn't sneaking photos of you. I wasn't!

228
14:02.625 --> 14:04.345
Sir! Sir, you haven't paid yet.

229
14:04.425 --> 14:05.265
Come on.

230
14:09.785 --> 14:11.145
Is paying really that important?

231
14:14.865 --> 14:15.745
I wasn't taking sneaky photos.

232
14:15.825 --> 14:17.385
They were just event photos.

233
14:17.465 --> 14:18.985
Besides, we're colleagues.

234
14:19.065 --> 14:20.785
Why make it so awkward?

235
14:21.305 --> 14:23.825
-We're just colleagues. -Exactly.

236
14:24.345 --> 14:25.945
Don't be so tense. Relax.

237
14:26.025 --> 14:27.425
It's such a nice afternoon.

238
14:27.505 --> 14:29.145
Let's talk about something fun--

239
14:29.225 --> 14:31.385
Is there anything fun to talk about with you?

240
14:31.465 --> 14:33.385
Every word you say is calculated.

241
14:34.105 --> 14:35.585
I've met plenty of people like you.

242
14:36.105 --> 14:37.145
Stop following me.

243
14:41.345 --> 14:42.185
What are you doing?

244
14:42.265 --> 14:43.265
When I was hurt,

245
14:43.345 --> 14:46.065
you started with that blunt confession to throw me off.

246
14:46.665 --> 14:47.545
Your last name is Bu.

247
14:48.345 --> 14:51.065
Marrying you would save me 50 years of work.

248
14:51.145 --> 14:53.745
Anyway, I don't have much to do outside work.

249
14:53.825 --> 14:54.745
So why don't I give it a shot?

250
14:55.265 --> 14:56.665
You helped me and praised me

251
14:56.745 --> 14:59.545
just to create contrast and leave an impression.

252
14:59.625 --> 15:01.945
You really think everyone is after your dad's money?

253
15:02.025 --> 15:05.065
You're pretty and capable.

254
15:05.145 --> 15:06.505
Can't I just be drawn to your personality?

255
15:06.585 --> 15:08.625
Then you laid out your sob story,

256
15:08.705 --> 15:12.385
making your past sound romantic and pitiful.

257
15:12.465 --> 15:14.625
Any soft-hearted girl would've fallen for it.

258
15:14.705 --> 15:16.785
You turned Hejun Management's six client-attraction tactics

259
15:16.865 --> 15:18.185
into a pick-up routine.

260
15:18.265 --> 15:19.505
Not bad at all.

261
15:22.665 --> 15:24.185
You saw right through me.

262
15:24.265 --> 15:25.665
This is embarrassing.

263
15:25.745 --> 15:27.265
Don't sell yourself short.

264
15:27.345 --> 15:31.145
These moves are more than enough for a simple, love-first girl.

265
15:31.985 --> 15:35.745
Too bad I know exactly the plays and agenda

266
15:36.265 --> 15:37.425
of scheming guys like you.

267
15:38.745 --> 15:39.745
You've been hurt before?

268
15:41.665 --> 15:43.985
-None of your business. -The trick doesn't have to be new.

269
15:44.505 --> 15:45.345
What matters is,

270
15:46.625 --> 15:47.465
did it work on you?

271
15:53.065 --> 15:56.065
I came to Maxmise to be a partner, not to date.

272
15:58.065 --> 15:59.425
You're already thinking about dating?

273
16:03.145 --> 16:04.345
Wait.

274
16:11.585 --> 16:12.625
Stop.

275
16:25.545 --> 16:26.465
Stop laughing.

276
16:39.745 --> 16:41.625
You're like a bobblehead.

277
16:48.625 --> 16:50.385
He used all six of Hejun's tactics on me.

278
16:50.465 --> 16:51.425
He's something else.

279
16:54.625 --> 16:55.465
Su Su?

280
16:58.905 --> 17:00.345
Sha Sha told me

281
17:01.185 --> 17:04.065
my client interface hasn't been proactive enough.

282
17:04.145 --> 17:07.585
My performance under pressure at the challenge camp was also just average.

283
17:07.665 --> 17:09.944
She suggested I transfer to the visualization team.

284
17:15.385 --> 17:16.985
The visualization team?

285
17:19.224 --> 17:22.305
It's the team that just does PowerPoint slides.

286
17:22.825 --> 17:24.184
Sounds fancy,

287
17:24.704 --> 17:27.944
but it's basically a demotion to back-office support.

288
17:28.025 --> 17:29.265
You can never come back to consulting.

289
17:30.425 --> 17:32.385
Isn't the challenge camp just a team-building thing?

290
17:32.465 --> 17:34.665
They actually use it as an evaluation tool?

291
17:34.745 --> 17:36.505
And what does "average under pressure" even mean?

292
17:36.585 --> 17:38.825
Su Su was sprinting while crying.

293
17:40.225 --> 17:41.305
You didn't know that?

294
17:41.905 --> 17:44.265
Using the challenge camp as a simulated test for the staff

295
17:44.345 --> 17:46.025
has always been a Maxmise tradition.

296
17:46.705 --> 17:49.425
The problem might be that she cried.

297
17:49.505 --> 17:52.705
In consulting, the last thing you want is to be emotional.

298
17:53.305 --> 17:54.905
It is what it is. Reality's harsh.

299
17:54.985 --> 17:56.065
It all comes down to ability.

300
18:00.185 --> 18:04.105
Oh, keep a close eye on the Bolo Culture project.

301
18:04.185 --> 18:06.265
You only get credit once the contract is actually signed.

302
18:06.985 --> 18:09.065
Do you think she'll quit?

303
18:09.665 --> 18:11.305
I'm guessing she will.

304
18:11.385 --> 18:13.425
Support departments are way behind business units

305
18:13.505 --> 18:15.265
in both status and pay.

306
18:15.865 --> 18:19.545
Within a week, someone new will take her place.

307
18:34.705 --> 18:35.545
Not bad.

308
18:36.225 --> 18:37.625
I approve of this proposal.

309
18:38.825 --> 18:39.705
So when can we sign?

310
18:41.225 --> 18:43.145
Send me the contract first. I'll have Legal review it.

311
18:43.225 --> 18:44.145
Okay.

312
18:44.665 --> 18:45.505
By the way,

313
18:45.585 --> 18:49.025
Maxmise isn't going to let a young girl like you handle

314
18:49.105 --> 18:50.305
a project this big alone, are they?

315
18:50.385 --> 18:51.905
Of course not.

316
18:51.985 --> 18:54.305
We'll set up a project team right after signing.

317
18:54.385 --> 18:56.545
With a project manager leading it,

318
18:56.625 --> 18:59.425
plus partners, consultants, data folks, and analysts like me.

319
19:03.505 --> 19:04.585
You're playing me.

320
19:05.105 --> 19:07.145
Payment is due after signing.

321
19:07.225 --> 19:08.065
So far,

322
19:08.145 --> 19:10.585
you've only come to our office for a few interviews

323
19:10.665 --> 19:11.705
and written some papers.

324
19:11.785 --> 19:13.705
All using your public templates.

325
19:13.785 --> 19:16.705
You don't even know what Qingyi Literature looks like

326
19:16.785 --> 19:18.345
or how many IPs they have.

327
19:18.425 --> 19:22.465
When our board asks me about the project's viability,

328
19:22.545 --> 19:23.665
what do I say?

329
19:24.185 --> 19:26.705
I've read a lot of Qingyi's iconic works,

330
19:26.785 --> 19:28.105
and I have all the IP library materials.

331
19:28.185 --> 19:29.225
But you're right.

332
19:29.305 --> 19:32.225
I'd love to join you for a site visit if that works for you.

333
19:32.305 --> 19:33.345
Perfect.

334
19:33.425 --> 19:35.825
I'm heading to their HQ tomorrow anyway.

335
19:35.905 --> 19:36.905
See you early tomorrow.

336
19:39.145 --> 19:40.385
Early tomorrow?

337
19:40.465 --> 19:42.265
Yeah. Flight leaves at 7 a.m.

338
19:42.345 --> 19:44.025
You have two hours to get ready.

339
19:48.145 --> 19:48.985
Hey, Zhao Heng.

340
19:49.065 --> 19:50.865
Got a sec to talk?

341
19:51.505 --> 19:53.345
Did you see my WeChat message?

342
19:53.425 --> 19:54.465
I have to take a last-minute business trip.

343
19:54.545 --> 19:57.465
I already applied through the system,

344
19:57.545 --> 19:58.825
and Ms. Lin approved it.

345
19:58.905 --> 20:01.585
Can you find the company travel reimbursement policy for me?

346
20:01.665 --> 20:03.945
I couldn't locate that file. Sure.

347
20:04.545 --> 20:06.065
Thanks. I know.

348
20:09.225 --> 20:09.825
NO VEHICLES AVAILABLE NEARBY

349
20:09.905 --> 20:10.705
YOUR ORDER HAS TIMED OUT PLEASE REQUEST A NEW RIDE

350
20:48.625 --> 20:49.545
Xu Chi!

351
20:54.265 --> 20:55.225
What's going on?

352
20:56.145 --> 20:58.105
Well, can you drop me at the subway station?

353
20:58.185 --> 20:59.345
I need to get to the airport.

354
20:59.425 --> 21:00.985
-Get in. -Great.

355
21:06.225 --> 21:07.545
Aren't you here on a business trip?

356
21:07.625 --> 21:09.505
Why are you driving yourself to the airport?

357
21:10.305 --> 21:11.865
Who said I'm on a business trip?

358
21:12.385 --> 21:14.665
-Thank you. -I'm based here from now on.

359
21:15.705 --> 21:17.585
I'm going to Hong Kong, China. Back tomorrow afternoon.

360
21:18.105 --> 21:19.785
Parking at the airport is convenient.

361
21:19.865 --> 21:21.465
Saves me from having an unreliable assistant

362
21:21.545 --> 21:22.665
pick me up wrong again.

363
21:31.865 --> 21:32.785
Where are you going?

364
21:33.625 --> 21:34.705
Guangzhou.

365
21:34.785 --> 21:36.305
I am doing research with a client.

366
21:36.385 --> 21:37.625
With your mentor?

367
21:38.785 --> 21:40.065
She told me to go alone.

368
21:40.905 --> 21:42.985
Didn't Maxmise assign you a new mentor?

369
21:43.865 --> 21:46.465
You can't become a consultant by figuring it all out on your own.

370
21:46.545 --> 21:48.905
This isn't a task for a newbie.

371
21:49.745 --> 21:50.705
I know.

372
21:51.265 --> 21:52.425
But I still want to try.

373
21:54.225 --> 21:57.225
By the way, I saw your suitcase earlier.

374
21:57.305 --> 21:58.145
It's cute.

375
21:59.265 --> 22:00.425
Really?

376
22:00.505 --> 22:01.585
I bought it in college.

377
22:01.665 --> 22:04.145
Let me give you some advice. Consultants should stick

378
22:04.225 --> 22:06.505
to a few well-known business brands for their suitcases.

379
22:06.585 --> 22:09.025
For women, go with a lightweight zippered fabric suitcase.

380
22:09.665 --> 22:11.385
It holds more and doesn't look bad if it gets scuffed.

381
22:11.465 --> 22:14.225
Stick to black, navy blue, or light brown.

382
22:14.305 --> 22:16.625
No bright colors. No cartoon stickers.

383
22:16.705 --> 22:18.105
Nothing over 20 inches.

384
22:18.185 --> 22:19.865
It must be carry-on size.

385
22:19.945 --> 22:21.425
It saves you from lost luggage

386
22:21.505 --> 22:24.705
and saves half an hour at check-in.

387
22:24.785 --> 22:28.825
A consultant charges clients 25,000 a day.

388
22:28.905 --> 22:29.745
Over ten hours,

389
22:29.825 --> 22:32.705
one trip saves you 2,500.

390
22:35.385 --> 22:36.785
But a carry-on is too small.

391
22:36.865 --> 22:38.065
What if the trip's over three days?

392
22:38.665 --> 22:40.785
Standard consultant setup is a canvas duffel

393
22:40.865 --> 22:41.905
on top of the suitcase,

394
22:42.505 --> 22:44.625
plus a backpack for your laptop.

395
22:44.705 --> 22:46.785
If you have time, go swap it out at the airport.

396
22:58.265 --> 22:59.625
Let me get it.

397
23:06.825 --> 23:08.145
Thank you so much.

398
23:09.385 --> 23:10.585
Let's add each other on WeChat.

399
23:10.665 --> 23:12.705
Your mentor's ignoring you anyway.

400
23:13.225 --> 23:15.865
If you have questions, I can be your off-site coach.

401
23:15.945 --> 23:16.825
Sure.

402
23:18.945 --> 23:20.545
Let me scan yours.

403
23:25.745 --> 23:27.625
YE THE LEGEND

404
23:29.465 --> 23:30.505
Ye the Legend?

405
23:31.745 --> 23:33.625
You give people nicknames this over-the-top now?

406
23:36.705 --> 23:37.705
It's not over-the-top.

407
23:38.305 --> 23:39.185
You're my idol.

408
23:40.065 --> 23:41.345
Oh nice, now you're laying it on thick.

409
23:41.425 --> 23:43.465
I'm not. I mean it.

410
23:45.745 --> 23:46.865
I…

411
23:48.145 --> 23:51.705
I've been trying hard to become a qualified consultant as soon as I can.

412
23:51.785 --> 23:54.745
Not just for the money and my mom's old apartment.

413
23:55.745 --> 23:58.065
I also hope that one day,

414
23:58.145 --> 24:01.545
I can be as strong and smart as you,

415
24:01.625 --> 24:04.265
stay calm, and handle anything with ease.

416
24:05.825 --> 24:07.025
With all that praise,

417
24:07.985 --> 24:08.825
you'll definitely make it.

418
24:08.905 --> 24:11.025
And this is your first business trip.

419
24:11.105 --> 24:12.985
So, don't expect to wow the client right away.

420
24:13.065 --> 24:14.305
Lower your expectations.

421
24:14.385 --> 24:17.305
Try to understand their real situation and what they truly need.

422
24:18.265 --> 24:19.945
I'm in a hurry to board. Bye.

423
24:32.505 --> 24:37.305
QINGYI LITERATURE

424
24:37.385 --> 24:38.345
That's not how you go about this!

425
24:38.425 --> 24:39.665
I don't agree with this plan. No way.

426
24:39.745 --> 24:40.585
We haven't even spoken yet,

427
24:40.665 --> 24:42.225
-and you're already jumping in? -All these rules and regulations…

428
24:42.305 --> 24:44.305
Just because you spoke first doesn't mean you're right. Right?

429
24:44.385 --> 24:46.385
I'm telling you, either you make it work, or forget it!

430
24:46.465 --> 24:47.545
I don't have much time!

431
24:47.625 --> 24:49.065
Whatever happens…

432
24:50.185 --> 24:51.825
-I don't care anymore. -Look what time it is!

433
24:51.905 --> 24:53.305
I'm going to miss my flight. That's it!

434
24:53.385 --> 24:54.465
Alright. Everyone, sit down!

435
24:55.105 --> 24:56.185
Are you done yet?

436
24:58.785 --> 25:00.785
This is a business negotiation, not a wet market.

437
25:04.505 --> 25:05.665
I have two more meetings this afternoon.

438
25:05.745 --> 25:07.025
I don't have time to do financial reports.

439
25:07.105 --> 25:10.065
-No, no. I don't have time. -Just let me see your previous ones.

440
25:11.025 --> 25:14.705
Mr. Li. Liu from our department will go to your office later

441
25:14.785 --> 25:15.625
to coordinate on the project.

442
25:15.705 --> 25:16.825
QINGYI LITERATURE

443
25:20.825 --> 25:22.385
So, what did you learn from this trip?

444
25:24.425 --> 25:26.665
I just went to see their senior management.

445
25:26.745 --> 25:28.385
They're not very willing to talk to me.

446
25:31.345 --> 25:33.185
I paid real money to acquire the company,

447
25:33.265 --> 25:35.505
and they're still paying lip service to me.

448
25:36.185 --> 25:38.145
You're a rookie who just showed up.

449
25:38.225 --> 25:40.665
And you asked their CFO for payroll reports.

450
25:40.745 --> 25:41.945
You think they'd give them to you?

451
25:46.185 --> 25:47.785
In my earlier proposal,

452
25:47.865 --> 25:51.265
I focused heavily on the senior executive compensation reform plan

453
25:51.345 --> 25:52.905
for Qingyi Literature.

454
25:52.985 --> 25:55.625
It emphasizes consistency, alignment, and granularity.

455
25:55.705 --> 25:57.545
-Once the project manager takes over-- -Hold on.

456
25:59.185 --> 26:02.145
Why are you talking like Lin Long with all that meaningless jargon?

457
26:02.225 --> 26:04.105
Are you trying to dazzle me with buzzwords?

458
26:04.185 --> 26:07.545
I'm telling you, that's what I saw internet investors do years ago.

459
26:08.985 --> 26:11.545
No. Bolo is a major internet company,

460
26:11.625 --> 26:13.585
so I wanted to use some industry terms.

461
26:13.665 --> 26:14.705
Enough. Stop explaining.

462
26:15.345 --> 26:17.105
I'm paying you consultants big money

463
26:17.185 --> 26:19.625
to help Qingyi Literature integrate into us smoothly.

464
26:20.305 --> 26:22.585
Yes, your arrangements for regular employees are not bad.

465
26:22.665 --> 26:26.065
But what I want is a more effective overall solution,

466
26:26.145 --> 26:28.825
not some simple compensation reform deck.

467
26:33.065 --> 26:33.945
Hello?

468
26:35.225 --> 26:36.305
Hold on.

469
26:36.385 --> 26:37.665
Alright. Let's leave it here for now.

470
26:37.745 --> 26:39.265
We'll catch up in Beijing when we have time.

471
26:43.505 --> 26:44.425
Go ahead.

472
26:50.145 --> 26:51.305
They have a lot of demands.

473
26:52.065 --> 26:53.945
Maxmise isn't helping much either.

474
26:54.985 --> 26:57.025
This acquisition is going to be tough.

475
27:06.545 --> 27:07.785
Your baby is fine,

476
27:07.865 --> 27:10.585
but you really need to rest and relax.

477
27:10.665 --> 27:14.745
Your spasmodic abdominal pain is closely linked to your emotional stress.

478
27:15.865 --> 27:16.785
Rest?

479
27:19.105 --> 27:20.185
Just wait a little longer.

480
27:24.825 --> 27:27.065
Ms. Lin, are you busy?

481
27:27.145 --> 27:29.185
Could you get back to me when you can? It's something urgent!

482
27:29.265 --> 27:30.705
Please get back to me as soon as you see this.

483
27:32.585 --> 27:37.905
LIN LONG

484
27:55.505 --> 27:57.185
MS. SHA SHA AT MAXMISE

485
28:00.385 --> 28:01.385
VOICE CALL

486
28:06.825 --> 28:08.265
Hello, Ms. Sha. This is Xu Chi.

487
28:08.345 --> 28:10.465
Sha Sha is on a video call with US headquarters.

488
28:10.545 --> 28:12.545
She asked me to take her call. What's up?

489
28:17.225 --> 28:19.385
It's about the Bolo Culture project.

490
28:19.465 --> 28:21.185
There are some things I don't understand and want to ask.

491
28:21.265 --> 28:24.305
You should be asking your mentor, not jumping the chain to Sha Sha.

492
28:24.905 --> 28:27.305
She doesn't have the obligation or time to mentor you.

493
28:29.905 --> 28:31.305
But Ms. Lin isn't answering my calls

494
28:31.825 --> 28:33.065
or emails or WeChat messages.

495
28:33.145 --> 28:35.825
Are you tattling like a grade-schooler now?

496
28:36.585 --> 28:40.025
Maxmise's policy is that everyone owns their own work.

497
28:40.105 --> 28:43.225
You took the Bolo Culture project from Lin Long.

498
28:43.305 --> 28:46.705
So you are fully responsible for its success or failure.

499
28:46.785 --> 28:48.385
The moment you chose to go solo,

500
28:48.465 --> 28:51.385
you lost the right to complain that your mentor isn't holding your hand.

501
28:51.465 --> 28:52.505
Good luck.

502
29:07.225 --> 29:08.665
XU CHI: MS. LIN, I HAVE AN URGENT ISSUE WITH BOLO CULTURE

503
29:10.225 --> 29:11.065
Check it now.

504
29:13.065 --> 29:14.225
No need.

505
29:14.305 --> 29:15.585
We agreed.

506
29:15.665 --> 29:17.425
Tonight I'm all yours.

507
29:18.745 --> 29:19.905
I've been taking the meds to keep the pregnancy safe.

508
29:19.985 --> 29:21.825
I'm in a much better place now.

509
29:21.905 --> 29:25.065
I really shouldn't have argued with you before.

510
29:27.145 --> 29:29.305
Honey. I'm sorry.

511
29:38.745 --> 29:42.545
I know you've been under a lot of pressure since I got pregnant.

512
29:43.385 --> 29:46.025
That day you came to the restaurant, you were thinking about the baby and me.

513
29:48.265 --> 29:50.305
But I don't know what came over me.

514
29:50.905 --> 29:53.305
I just can't control my emotions.

515
29:53.385 --> 29:55.625
-Sometimes I feel like I'm-- -Alright.

516
29:55.705 --> 29:57.105
Don't blame yourself.

517
29:57.625 --> 29:59.025
It's normal to have mood swings during pregnancy.

518
29:59.625 --> 30:02.785
I just hope you don't put too much energy into work.

519
30:03.305 --> 30:04.985
Don't worry. I won't anymore.

520
30:05.065 --> 30:07.065
I've already talked to the company.

521
30:07.585 --> 30:08.705
I'm pregnant.

522
30:08.785 --> 30:11.065
From now on, I'll avoid overtime as much as I can.

523
30:11.145 --> 30:13.985
I'll start my maternity leave 30 days before my due date.

524
30:14.065 --> 30:16.825
And after the baby's born, I'll make more time for family.

525
30:16.905 --> 30:19.465
I promise to raise him to be as smart as you.

526
30:21.145 --> 30:23.825
Honestly, I've never been against you working.

527
30:23.905 --> 30:25.265
A second income is a good thing.

528
30:25.905 --> 30:27.625
But consulting is exhausting.

529
30:27.705 --> 30:28.825
And you're always working late.

530
30:29.345 --> 30:31.905
Why not switch to something easier?

531
30:34.225 --> 30:35.705
What's more important, family or work?

532
30:35.785 --> 30:37.665
Family, of course.

533
30:38.345 --> 30:40.585
What matters most is that we build a good life together.

534
30:40.665 --> 30:41.625
Right?

535
30:43.905 --> 30:45.745
Come on. Have some fish.

536
30:54.585 --> 30:55.985
This is your first business trip.

537
30:56.065 --> 30:58.145
So, don't expect to wow the client right away.

538
30:58.225 --> 30:59.345
Lower your expectations.

539
30:59.425 --> 31:03.265
Try to understand their real situation and what they truly need.

540
31:04.785 --> 31:08.345
Can you just tell us straight up what we actually need to do

541
31:08.425 --> 31:11.865
to get the veteran Qingyi employees to integrate into our group,

542
31:11.945 --> 31:13.385
fall in line,

543
31:13.905 --> 31:16.345
and most importantly, stay motivated at the same time?

544
31:17.465 --> 31:18.665
We haven't even spoken yet,

545
31:18.745 --> 31:19.505
-and you're already jumping in? -All these rules and regulations

546
31:19.585 --> 31:20.345
don't fit our company's growth!

547
31:20.425 --> 31:21.585
-I have two more meetings this afternoon. -Just because you spoke first…

548
31:21.665 --> 31:22.985
-I don't have time for financial reports. -I'm telling you,

549
31:23.065 --> 31:24.705
either you make it work or forget it!

550
31:25.425 --> 31:28.225
Your arrangements for regular employees are not bad,

551
31:28.305 --> 31:31.985
but what I want is a more effective overall solution,

552
31:32.505 --> 31:35.225
not some simple compensation reform deck.

553
31:41.625 --> 31:44.425
MIDDLE AND LOWER MANAGEMENT

554
31:46.625 --> 31:48.705
What was it that convinced him last time?

555
31:49.345 --> 31:50.705
Since your company isn't short on cash,

556
31:50.785 --> 31:53.585
and all you care about is Qingyi's IPs,

557
31:53.665 --> 31:55.185
why not start fresh?

558
31:55.265 --> 31:56.545
Go on.

559
32:03.305 --> 32:04.785
SENIOR MANAGEMENT

560
32:04.865 --> 32:06.745
Keep the senior executives for now.

561
32:12.465 --> 32:13.825
MR. SHEN, BOLO CULTURE

562
32:16.185 --> 32:17.505
CALL

563
32:18.425 --> 32:20.985
VIDEO CALL, VOICE CALL

564
32:27.985 --> 32:31.865
YE THE LEGEND

565
32:37.665 --> 32:39.585
Richard. Can I ask you something?

566
32:39.665 --> 32:42.185
It's about the project I'm on during this business trip.

567
32:42.265 --> 32:44.905
Maxmise is helping Bolo Culture with organizational efficiency.

568
32:44.985 --> 32:47.185
We had good communication with their leadership before,

569
32:47.265 --> 32:51.265
but their boss just blew up and rejected the whole proposal.

570
32:51.345 --> 32:52.545
See image.

571
32:59.865 --> 33:01.105
So, as my interviewer,

572
33:01.625 --> 33:04.505
teach me how to land a big deal like Tianhe Air.

573
33:05.185 --> 33:07.345
Our firms are competitors.

574
33:07.425 --> 33:08.385
That's confidential.

575
33:08.465 --> 33:09.305
Can I just tell you that?

576
33:09.905 --> 33:11.585
Then why did you teach me how to pick restaurants?

577
33:12.185 --> 33:13.665
Most people don't need to be taught that.

578
33:14.265 --> 33:15.185
Wait.

579
33:16.025 --> 33:18.545
If I ask him every time I hit a problem,

580
33:19.305 --> 33:21.385
isn't that just cheating with a walkthrough?

581
33:24.905 --> 33:26.105
RECALL THE MESSAGE

582
33:26.705 --> 33:27.785
MESSAGE RECALLED

583
33:29.825 --> 33:32.585
COULD I ASK YOU FOR SOME ADVICE, RICHARD?

584
33:38.345 --> 33:39.385
Who are you texting?

585
33:41.345 --> 33:42.785
One second you're frowning, and the next you're smiling.

586
33:42.865 --> 33:43.945
Got a crush or something?

587
33:45.265 --> 33:46.105
Just a young lady

588
33:46.185 --> 33:47.305
in the same industry as us.

589
33:47.825 --> 33:49.665
She sent me a long WeChat message earlier.

590
33:49.745 --> 33:51.945
Probably felt something she said wasn't right,

591
33:52.025 --> 33:53.945
so she recalled it and went to revise it.

592
33:54.665 --> 33:56.585
A young lady?

593
33:58.545 --> 34:00.625
I… I've seen her before.

594
34:00.705 --> 34:01.665
Right here.

595
34:01.745 --> 34:03.705
You sat here, and she sat there. The one I saw.

596
34:05.065 --> 34:06.705
Oh my goodness, Ye.

597
34:06.785 --> 34:07.825
You're really something.

598
34:07.905 --> 34:10.025
Such a young girlfriend.

599
34:10.105 --> 34:11.065
Stop it.

600
34:11.145 --> 34:13.385
I genuinely think she's talented.

601
34:14.025 --> 34:15.465
And her work style

602
34:15.545 --> 34:19.264
and the problems she runs into remind me of myself back then.

603
34:20.304 --> 34:22.304
I took a lot of wrong turns.

604
34:22.385 --> 34:26.025
I don't want her to make the same mistakes.

605
34:27.304 --> 34:30.985
So, when are you starting your plan?

606
34:31.065 --> 34:33.225
Just say the word if you need anything from me.

607
34:36.465 --> 34:38.505
That's actually why I asked you to come today.

608
34:43.065 --> 34:46.945
FOLIC ACID TABLETS

609
34:54.185 --> 34:56.505
Sure enough. Got him a new graphics card and he's happy.

610
34:56.585 --> 34:58.385
He's downloading games like crazy now.

611
34:58.465 --> 35:00.025
That's good.

612
35:00.105 --> 35:02.625
Couples shouldn't stay in a cold war forever.

613
35:02.705 --> 35:04.345
And think about it.

614
35:04.425 --> 35:05.745
When you're in the delivery room,

615
35:05.825 --> 35:07.865
if he makes a decision while angry,

616
35:07.945 --> 35:09.265
you'll be the one suffering for life.

617
35:10.145 --> 35:11.105
It's fine now.

618
35:11.185 --> 35:12.665
He's happy, and you're happy.

619
35:13.665 --> 35:15.345
But I'm not happy at all.

620
35:15.425 --> 35:17.185
I actually feel kind of sad.

621
35:18.425 --> 35:21.025
Tactics like playing weak and pleasing people

622
35:21.105 --> 35:22.505
are what I used to use on clients.

623
35:22.585 --> 35:23.785
But now?

624
35:23.865 --> 35:28.145
Now I have to use them on a man I once loved.

625
35:29.305 --> 35:30.305
Don't overthink it.

626
35:31.785 --> 35:32.945
But I'm not giving up.

627
35:33.465 --> 35:34.465
Once this phase is over,

628
35:34.545 --> 35:38.225
I'm taking back everything I've given up.

629
35:38.305 --> 35:40.305
You still want Xu Chi out?

630
35:40.825 --> 35:42.865
Take it easy.

631
35:42.945 --> 35:46.905
I already gave her low scores in the newbie challenge camp.

632
35:47.665 --> 35:49.905
Don't worry. I've let it go.

633
35:49.985 --> 35:51.785
If she wants to fight, fine by me.

634
35:51.865 --> 35:54.985
But I'm not giving her any useful guidance or advice anymore.

635
35:55.065 --> 35:58.265
At most, I'll reply to her emails with a "You can try."

636
36:00.025 --> 36:02.825
Does she really think making slide decks is all it takes to be a consultant?

637
36:02.905 --> 36:05.305
This industry runs on experience.

638
36:05.385 --> 36:09.065
Without a mentor walking you through real-world projects,

639
36:09.145 --> 36:10.785
even a genius is all theory and no practice.

640
36:19.625 --> 36:20.505
Mr. Shen.

641
36:21.105 --> 36:21.945
What are you doing here?

642
36:22.025 --> 36:23.705
I was afraid it'd be too late by the time I got to Beijing.

643
36:23.785 --> 36:25.585
So now's a good time to talk.

644
36:26.385 --> 36:28.185
This is the second version of the proposal I rushed out.

645
36:28.265 --> 36:29.345
Please take a look.

646
36:31.065 --> 36:32.945
"Streamline the HR structure."

647
36:33.025 --> 36:36.545
"Hollow out Qingyi Literature's existing senior management?"

648
36:36.625 --> 36:38.185
If I'm not mistaken,

649
36:38.265 --> 36:41.545
you're looking to address not just Qingyi's middle and lower management,

650
36:41.625 --> 36:42.465
but also the senior level.

651
36:44.185 --> 36:46.785
So your consulting needs have changed.

652
36:48.225 --> 36:49.265
Have a seat.

653
36:52.345 --> 36:57.905
You acquired Qingyi Literature just for their IPs, right?

654
36:57.985 --> 37:00.145
But because Qingyi has too many employees,

655
37:00.225 --> 37:04.265
you're worried they'll affect Bolo's corporate culture.

656
37:04.345 --> 37:06.985
That's why you brought in Maxmise.

657
37:07.065 --> 37:09.265
You want them to integrate without causing you any trouble.

658
37:10.145 --> 37:13.185
My initial plan to lay off all of Qingyi's middle and lower management

659
37:13.265 --> 37:14.305
appealed to you

660
37:14.385 --> 37:17.145
because it offered a clean, quick solution.

661
37:17.825 --> 37:18.785
Keep the senior executives for now.

662
37:18.865 --> 37:20.465
Let all other former Qingyi employees leave

663
37:20.545 --> 37:22.065
with the market's best severance package

664
37:22.145 --> 37:23.745
of 2N plus 10.

665
37:23.825 --> 37:25.505
But gradually, you realized

666
37:25.585 --> 37:28.105
that Qingyi's senior management is also a liability.

667
37:28.185 --> 37:29.065
You want to deal with them too.

668
37:29.145 --> 37:31.265
-You're already jumping in? -All these rules and regulations…

669
37:31.345 --> 37:32.585
-I am telling you… -Nonsense!

670
37:33.385 --> 37:35.825
Either you make it work or forget it!

671
37:36.705 --> 37:38.185
But on a conscious level,

672
37:38.265 --> 37:41.465
you might not have been able to articulate what you actually needed.

673
37:41.545 --> 37:45.065
That's why you blew up at me this afternoon.

674
37:45.145 --> 37:47.025
I'm paying you consultants big money

675
37:47.105 --> 37:49.785
to help Qingyi Literature integrate into us smoothly.

676
37:49.865 --> 37:52.145
Not some simple compensation reform deck.

677
37:54.825 --> 37:56.985
Looks like you know me better than I know myself.

678
37:58.225 --> 38:00.625
In the future, you could not only do management consulting,

679
38:00.705 --> 38:01.865
but also moonlight as a shrink.

680
38:04.105 --> 38:07.025
Either way, consulting is essentially a personal service.

681
38:07.785 --> 38:09.625
We use our own experience to help clients

682
38:09.705 --> 38:11.665
analyze problems from an outside perspective.

683
38:11.745 --> 38:15.345
To help you see the elephant in the room you couldn't see before.

684
38:15.945 --> 38:16.825
But regardless,

685
38:16.905 --> 38:19.985
I owe you an apology for that outburst this afternoon.

686
38:20.865 --> 38:21.825
But as the client,

687
38:21.905 --> 38:23.185
I'm allowed to be a little temperamental.

688
38:23.265 --> 38:24.905
-You can forgive that, right? -Of course.

689
38:25.425 --> 38:29.025
Set up an overseas business unit headquartered in Singapore.

690
38:29.105 --> 38:31.465
Transfer all of Qingyi's senior management there.

691
38:32.545 --> 38:34.745
If they can't integrate into Bolo's culture,

692
38:34.825 --> 38:36.265
just ship them all overseas.

693
38:36.345 --> 38:38.905
First, Bolo is expanding its overseas business.

694
38:38.985 --> 38:43.065
Second, most of Qingyi's senior managers have kids in primary or middle school.

695
38:43.585 --> 38:47.145
If you offer a good title, solid pay, and great benefits,

696
38:47.225 --> 38:49.585
their families will push them to go.

697
38:49.665 --> 38:51.305
It's an overseas degree, after all.

698
38:51.825 --> 38:54.865
Third, if they actually make something of themselves over there,

699
38:54.945 --> 38:57.065
it's a win for Bolo too.

700
38:58.745 --> 39:00.585
-Interesting. -Of course,

701
39:00.665 --> 39:02.665
the formal proposal won't be written exactly like this.

702
39:02.745 --> 39:05.425
You just need to understand the real purpose of this consulting engagement.

703
39:06.465 --> 39:07.305
Mr. Shen, I promise

704
39:07.385 --> 39:10.265
Maxmise will put together a top-notch consulting team.

705
39:10.345 --> 39:11.425
We'll craft a solution that covers everything,

706
39:11.505 --> 39:13.305
from potential restructuring and vision-driven strategy

707
39:13.385 --> 39:15.465
to scaling your ecosystem and business model overseas.

708
39:15.545 --> 39:17.425
We'll make sure most of Bolo and Qingyi's employees

709
39:17.505 --> 39:19.025
are on board and happy with the outcome.

710
39:19.105 --> 39:22.305
That way, your consulting fees are money well spent.

711
39:23.825 --> 39:26.025
I like your big words this time.

712
39:28.545 --> 39:29.785
Tell me more.
